@talks saruth
// TW1, the Talk a while pack: Envoy Saruth's own talks (they/them). Formal and exact, NO contractions; unhurried;
// names small courtesies; a dry joke a sentence late. Guests don't draw the pool, so Saruth has these, then small
// talk. Never why they were sent (until close); never Veyli rites in full; never a nickname before close.

== knock-twice
topic: ship
them: May I ask you something about your people? You knock twice. Always twice. Never once.
them: I have counted. Not one human aboard knocks three times. It is very consistent.   #funny
ask: Why twice? I would like the true answer, if there is one.
listen: How do the Veyli ask to come in?
  them: A cord on the door. Tied loose, you are expected. Otherwise, by invitation only.
share: Once is an accident. Twice is a person.
  them: Ah. That is a good answer. I will write it down. Thank you.   #warm
cheer: Three is showing off.
  them: ... Yes. I see. That was a joke. I have caught it. Late, but I have it.   #funny

== tea-hour
topic: day
when: tier>=acquaintance
them: Each day I take tea at the same hour. Kneeling, at a low table. Your crew find it strange.
them: To me, the strange thing is your tea queue. Everyone, at once, standing, in a hurry.   #funny
ask: Is there something you do at the same hour every day?
listen: What does the hour mean, for you?
  them: That the day has a still place in it. However the rest goes. It is not a small thing.
share: Breakfast. Same seat, most days.
  them: Then you understand. A fixed point is a kindness you give yourself.   #warm
cheer: Get lost on Deck 2. Reliably.
  them: That is also a ritual. A very human one. I have seen several of you perform it.   #funny

== seedlings
topic: hobby
when: tier>=colleague
them: I keep Veyli seedlings in a corner of the garden. Cruz waters them when I forget.
them: I never forget. Cruz waters them anyway. I have decided this is affection.   #warm
ask: What do your people do, when they want to show someone they care?
listen: Do the seedlings like it here?
  them: They lean towards the lamps. All of them, the same way. Like juniors at dinner.   #funny
share: Feed them. Or sit with them.
  them: We sit. Often without speaking. Your people find the silence hard. You do not, I notice.   #warm
cheer: Bring biscuits. Always biscuits.
  them: Chef Brennan has explained biscuits to me. At length. I accept them now.   #funny

== exhausting
topic: crew
when: tier>=friend
them: May I tell you something I have not said to the Captain? Your people are exhausting.
them: And very kind. Often at once. I did not expect both. I am still deciding what to do.
ask: And the Veyli? What do you find hardest about my people? Be honest.
listen: What's hardest about us, for you?
  them: The noise. Everyone speaks, all the time, kindly. I have learned to listen faster.
share: I don't know you well enough yet.
  them: An honest answer. Then we are both still learning. I find that a comfort.   #warm
cheer: The coffee. It has opinions.
  them: Chief Holt says the same of me. I take it as a compliment. He does not.   #funny
